sn12.24:3.2 starts: some ascetics and brahmins, proponents of kamma,
sn12.24:5.2 starts: Also, in the case of those ascetics and brahmins, proponents of kamma,
sn12.24:6.2 starts: Also, in the case of those ascetics and brahmins, proponents of kamma,
sn12.24:21.9 starts: But with the remainderless fading away and cessation
sn22.79:1.3 starts: What five?
sn22.79:1.4 starts: “When recollecting thus, bhikkhus: ‘I had such form
sn22.79:1.5 starts: it is just form that one recollects.
sn22.79:1.6 starts: When recollecting: ‘I had such a feeling
sn22.79:1.8 starts: When recollecting: ‘I had such a perception
sn22.79:1.9 starts: When recollecting: ‘I had such volitional formations
sn22.79:1.10 starts: When recollecting: ‘I had such consciousness
sn22.79:1.11 starts: it is just consciousness that one recollects.
sn22.79:5.2 starts: ‘They construct the conditioned,’ bhikkhus, therefore they are called volitional formations. And
sn22.79:9.2 starts: ‘I am now being devoured by volitional formations.’
sn22.79:9.8 starts: …
sn22.79:10.1 starts: ‘I am now being devoured by consciousness.
sn22.79:10.2 starts: In the past too I was devoured by consciousness in the very same way
sn22.79:12.3 starts: who scatters and does not amass;
sn22.79:12.4 starts: who extinguishes and does not kindle.
sn22.79:14.15 starts: He neither scatters nor amasses form, but abides
sn22.79:14.16 starts: He neither scatters nor amasses feeling …
sn22.89:13.3 starts: And the Venerable Khemaka has explained, taught
